{{for|league|Legion league}}
[[File:Legion screenshot.jpg|right|thumb|A player fighting two combatting legions.]]
'''Legions''' are ancient armies frozen in the midst of battle. They can be encountered by touching a '''Timeless Monolith''', which breaks out the Legions and gives the player a window of time to defeat them. This encounter is considered [[Extra Content]] and has a baseline 8% chance to appear in any non-unique [[map]] area.

==Overview==
[[File:Legion General monolith indicator.webp|thumb|A purple indicator on an activated Legion Monolith pointing in the direction of a Legion General, as well as the Legion timer.]]
[[File:Legion Schism.jpg|right|thumb|The Schism progress bar during a Legion encounter.]]
Players can find a Legion by interacting with a Timeless Monolith. Monoliths have a base greater than 8% chance to spawn in a [[map]].

Monoliths can also be found via other sources:
* By use of a {{il|Legion Scarab}}
* As a room in [[The Temple of Atzoatl]] (the [[Hall of Mettle]] room and its upgraded versions).  
* In [[The Climb]] (Act 1) - Will always have Eternal and Karui legions
* In [[The Dried Lake]] (Act 4) - Will always have an Eternal legion

Interacting with the Monolith will reveal a battle between two Legion factions that are in stasis. A timer will start once the Monolith is activated. During this phase, the enemies can be "killed", breaking them out of stasis and allowing them to be fought when the timer ends for rewards. The timer can range from 14 to 20 seconds (or more with Atlas passives), with a longer timer in lower-level zones. Once the timer runs out, all the enemies that were broken out of stasis will remain and start attacking. Killing 90% of the monsters, including all sergeants, generals, and chests, will break out all Legion monsters early. Enemies that didn't get broken out will disappear.

Some Legion enemies are marked as Sergeants and have a symbol above their heads that indicate an additional reward type they will drop. [[Chest]]s and War Hoards can be damaged while in stasis and will break out nearby non-sergeants/generals when "killed". The general of each Legion can occasionally spawn, always spawning in the far rear of the formation. If a general spawns, the monolith will display a wave of purple on the bottom in the direction of the general.

'''Schism''': Alternatively, taking the [[Timeless Conflict]] keystone will disable the Legion timer. Instead, breaking out monsters and chests from stasis will contribute progress towards a Schism, as shown by a progress bar. Once the progress bar is full, the Schism will occur and the Legion encounter will begin. Breaking out monsters and chests with rewards or more powerful monsters will contribute more progress towards the Schism.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3408278#8</ref>

Generally, rarer, more rewarding spawns will spawn further away from the monolith. Therefore, it's advised to move deep into a formation as quickly as possible if you are looking for rare spawns.

==Mechanics==
'''Rarity''': Legion Sergeants are rare monsters whereas Legion Generals are unique monsters.

==Items==
There are two types of currency associated with monoliths; each are specific to the legion.

===Splinters===
{{main|Splinter}}
Legion enemies and chests can drop Splinters of their Legion. 100 Splinters of the same type can be combined into an Emblem.

{{Query base item
|where=items.class_id="StackableCurrency" AND items.name LIKE "%Splinter%" AND items.help_text LIKE "%Emblem%"
|large=1
|drop_level=1
|stack_size=100
|stack_size_currency_tab=1
|help_text=1
}}

===Emblems===
{{main|Emblem}}
Emblems are obtained from combining [[Splinter]]s. They can be put into a [[map device]] in order to open a portal to the [[Domain of Timeless Conflict]]. You must use at least two Emblems of different Legions to open a portal to the Domain.

{{Query base item
|where=items.class_id="MapFragment" AND items.name LIKE "%Emblem%"
|large=1
|drop_level=1
|help_text=1
|description=1
}}

===Enshrouding crystal===
{{main|Enshrouding crystal}}
Using an [[enshrouding crystal]] on a [[unique item]] will enshroud them. Enshrouded uniques can be taken to the [[Domain of Timeless Conflict]] and inserted into a Crystal of Permutation and charged by up killing enemies during the encounter. Once it has reached a certain kill threshold, the crystal can be broken to receive a [[Vestigial unique item]] that has an implicit modifier based on the enshrouded unique.

Enshrouding crystals can drop from Legion Generals during regular Legion encounters.

{{Item table
|where = items.name LIKE "%Enshrouding Crystal%"
|large=1
|description=1
|drop_text=1
}}

====Timeless jewels====
The following unique timeless jewels drop exclusively in the [[Domain of Timeless Conflict]], or extremely rarely from Legion Generals from regular Legion encounters.
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|where=items.base_item = "Timeless Jewel" AND items.drop_text LIKE "%Timeless Conflict%"
|base_item=1
|large=1
|level=1
|stat=1
}}

