==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.30.0|
* Reduced the amount that breaking out Legion monsters and chests causes a Schism by approximately 33%.
* Each percentage of increased Atlas Drops increases the quantity of Maps and Threads found in the area by 1%. Additionally it increases the chance for additional drops from specific monsters within Maps, such as the chance to drop a Conqueror's Exalted Orb from a Conqueror Boss or Splinters from Legion monsters.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.29.0|
* Legion encounters will now automatically break out all Monsters in the encounter if you have broken out 90% of the total Monsters, as well as Chests, Sergeants, and Generals.
* Incubators no longer be obtained. Existing Incubators and Incubated items in Standard Leagues are unaffected by this change.
* Timeless Splinters can no longer drop outside of Legion encounters and Maps completed by Kingsmarch Atlas Runners.
* Legion Generals now drop more Timeless Splinters on average.
* Non-Sergeant, non-General Legion Monsters no longer drop Timeless Splinters.
* Sergeants and Chests now have a lower chance to drop Timeless Splinters, but now drop them in higher stack sizes.
* Lowered the effect of Map Item Quantity on the chances for Sergeants and Chests to drop Timeless Splinters.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.28.0|
* Possessed Legion Monsters can no longer release [[Tormented Spirit]]s when being broken out. They can still release Tormented Spirits once broken out.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.24.0|
* The fifth [[Map Device|map device]] slot is now unlocked by completing any [[tier 17 map]] instead of 4-way Domain of Timeless Conflict.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.23.0|
* Metamorph rewards from [[Heist]], [[Expedition]], [[Immortal Syndicate|Betrayal]], Delirium, [[Legion]] and [[Eldritch Altar]]s have been replaced with Ultimatum rewards.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.20.0|
* We want to improve on the concept that the Atlas Tree allows players to invest into leagues that they enjoy, and have added new clusters to the passive tree for league content that can be blocked through Atlas Passive Skills. We've also increased the chances for such league content to appear.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.18.1|
* Time-frozen Legion monsters can no longer be empowered by Sentinels.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.16.0|
* Many Legion Monsters have had the maximum distance they are able to use their long-ranged skills reduced, or can no longer use their long-ranged skills against other Legion Monsters.
* Legion no longer spawns in [[Delve]]. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.13.1|
* Legion monsters are no longer revived in Ritual encounters.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.0|
* Reduced the chance for Map Areas to contain [[Abyss]], [[Strongbox|Ambush]], [[Blight (game mechanic)|Blight]], [[Breach (original)|Breach]], [[Shrine|Domination]], [[Essence]], [[Smuggler's Cache|Heist]], [[Legion]], [[Metamorph]] and [[Tormented spirit|Torment]] encounters by 20%. The chance to encounter a Zana mission containing any of these mechanics has also been lowered by the same amount.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.12.0|
* The [[Buried Monolith]] encounter ('''Legion''') is now restricted to areas of level 68 and above.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.8.0|
* You can now encounter Legion in the following ways:
** As a new possible Incursion room, with each tier increasing the potential value of the Legion encounter in the eventual Temple of Atzoatl.
** As a rare Delve encounter.
** As a random encounter within the Atlas (10% chance in each Map).
** In addition to the above ways of encountering Legion monoliths, you can now find Legion uniques in chests that award league-restricted items.
* Vagan now awards various Legion-related items in Betrayal Safehouses. In Transportation Safehouses he awards Legion Splinters. In Research he awards Incubators. In Intervention he awards Legion Scarabs. In Fortification he awards a set of chests that can be found in Legion encounters.
* Unique items that can be found exclusively from Legion encounters as of 3.7.0 can still only be found from Legion encounters and the related reward sources above.
* Time-frozen Legion monsters who are afflicted by a proliferating [[Ignite]], and similar lingering effects, will no longer remove that Ignite upon being broken out.
}}
